From 134e4e0d297aebca0cf0ea18268f09211ad2c51f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PhialsBasement <PhialsBasement@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 31 May 2026 17:11:52 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] msvcrt: Avoid NULL dereference in _FindAndUnlinkFrame on an
 empty frame list.

When data->frame_info_head is NULL (no registered frames) and the frame
being unlinked is not the head, the lookup loop dereferenced a NULL
pointer via cur->next. Photoshop 2021's C++ exception handling triggers
__CxxUnregisterExceptionObject with an empty frame list, faulting on a
read at offset 8. Guard the loop against a NULL current frame so it falls
through to the existing "frame not found" path instead of crashing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/msvcrt/except.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/msvcrt/except.c b/dlls/msvcrt/except.c
index 8be9ab7c785..3ebdcdb0bb3 100644
--- a/dlls/msvcrt/except.c
+++ b/dlls/msvcrt/except.c
@@ -919,7 +919,7 @@ void CDECL _FindAndUnlinkFrame(frame_info *fi)
         return;
     }
 
-    for (; cur->next; cur = cur->next)
+    for (; cur && cur->next; cur = cur->next)
     {
         if (cur->next == fi)
         {
